Two and a half hours later Autumn and Violet walked into the club. 

Purple lights swirled around the first floor. Bodies swayed to the heavy bass of the music.  The DJ was on a platform the the left that looked large enough for a live band. To the right a long padded bench lined the wall with small a small table and chair placed ever four feet or so for additional seating.  Behind the long padded bench was the stairway to the second floor. Straight ahead was the bar.  
I know where I’m headed first. Autumn said nodding toward the bar.
Shots! Shots! Shots! Good idea Violet agreed as they both started to weave there way through the sea of people on the dance floor.

Two vodka shots later Autumn felt a tingle down her back as if someone had caressed her. She turned around looking for the asshole who tried to cop a feel but no one was there.  Still she felt something.
